  "headline": "Varga's early blast and an eighth-inning rally sink the Foxes",
  "narrative": "The Foxes scored first on a two-out double in the top of the first. <em>Mateo Varga</em> answered with a two-run homer in the second, and after the Foxes went back ahead in the fifth, <em>June Okafor</em> singled in the tying run and <em>Dell Brannigan</em> broke the tie with a solo shot in the sixth. In the eighth, <em>Ravi Castellanos</em> singled home a run and <em>Varga</em> added a sacrifice fly to stretch the lead to three. <em>Gus Pemberton</em> worked around a single in the ninth to close out a 6–3 win at Tidewater Park.",
  "playerNotes": [
    {
      "name": "Mateo Varga",
      "note": "Mateo Varga drove in half the offense — a two-run homer in the second and a sacrifice fly in the eighth."
    },
    {
      "name": "June Okafor",
      "note": "June Okafor reached three times, singled in the tying run in the fifth and scored twice from the leadoff spot."
    },
    {
      "name": "Dell Brannigan",
      "note": "Dell Brannigan's only hit was the one that mattered: a solo homer that put the Herons ahead for good."
    },
    {
      "name": "Ravi Castellanos",
      "note": "Ravi Castellanos added two hits, including the RBI single that opened the eighth-inning cushion."
    }
  ],
  "pitching": {
    "starter": "<em>Sam Whitlock</em> went six innings and struck out seven, leaning harder on his slider than usual. He gave up three runs on five hits, two of them in a fifth inning that briefly put the Foxes back in front. That kept him close to his season form — a 3.41 ERA and a 1.12 WHIP.",
    "bullpen": "<em>Theo Marchetti</em>, <em>Alana Reyes</em> and <em>Gus Pemberton</em> each took one inning and combined for three scoreless frames on two hits. <em>Reyes</em> struck out two in the eighth before <em>Pemberton</em> closed it out.",
